{{Quote|I'm Cobb Vanth. Lawman and de facto mayor of what used to be Mos Pelgo.''"<br />"''Freetown, now.|Cobb Vanth and [[Issa-Or]]|<ref name="Life Debt" />}}
'''Freetown''',<ref name="Chapter 6" /> formerly known as '''Mos Pelgo''',<ref name="Chapter 9">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 9: The Marshal}}</ref> and also known as '''Free City''',<ref name="Lando">{{EncyclopediaCite|Lando Calrissian and Other Characters From the Galaxy}}</ref> was a [[City|town]]<ref name="Life Debt" /> located in the northern hemisphere of the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]].<ref name="CVD">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref> In [[4 ABY]],<ref name="4 ABY">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' states that [[Temmin Wexley]] and [[Norra Wexley]] were reunited on [[Akiva]], which took place in the novel [[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']], thirty [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Hosnian Cataclysm|Starkiller incident]], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[34 ABY]]. Therefore, the events of ''Aftermath'' must have taken place in [[4 ABY]].</ref> the [[Mining Collective]] rounded up the citizens of the town for labor, with one man,<ref name="Chapter 9">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 9: The Marshal}}</ref> [[Sheriff]]<ref name="Aftermath" /> [[Cobb Vanth]], stealing a [[camtono]] of [[silicax oxalate]] crystals from them before fleeing into the [[desert]]. Vanth eventually encountered a [[Jawa]] [[sandcrawler]] and traded the crystals for a [[Boba Fett's armor|set of]] [[Mandalorian armor]].<ref name="Chapter 9" /> Soon after, the [[miner]] and representative of the newly established organization [[Red Key Raiders|Red Key Company]] [[Adwin Charu]] arrived to barter with the Jawas. When Charu tried to claim the armor for himself, Vanth shot him before leaving.<ref name="Aftermath" /> Returning to Mos Pelgo, he single-handedly [[Liberation of Mos Pelgo|liberated the town]] from the Mining Collective.<ref name="Chapter 9" /> He became the de facto [[mayor]] and protector of the town.<ref name="Life Debt" />

[[File:CadBaneWarning-BOBFCE.png|thumb|left|300px|Bane warned the townsfolk to not interfere with the Pyke Syndicate.]]
The city became known as Freetown<ref name="Life Debt" /> and was the site of a [[Skirmish in Freetown|battle]] between the Red Key Raiders and Vanth's allies.<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref> Later, Vanth defended the people from [[Tusken Raider]]s, who attacked their village.<ref name="Chapter 9" /> By [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date 9 ABY">{{MandoDate|9}}</ref> the town was once again known as Mos Pelgo. The [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] traveled to Mos Pelgo searching for another Mandalorian. After meeting Vanth, he acquired his armor after helping him [[Mission to Tatooine (Din Djarin)|slay]] a [[krayt dragon]] that had been killing Mos Pelgo's livestock.<ref name="Chapter 9" /> After this victory, the town was once again renamed Freetown. Djarin later returned to the town, and requested Vanth to assist [[Boba Fett]] in his fight against the [[Pyke Syndicate]]. After Djarin left, [[Cad Bane]] arrived at the town, and shot [[deputy]] [[Scott]] and Vanth.<ref name="Chapter 6" /> The town's [[Freetown garrison|garrison]] later joined the [[Battle of Mos Espa|battle]] against the [[Pyke]]s in revenge.<ref name="Chapter 7">{{BOBF|Chapter 7: In the Name of Honor}}</ref> A drink known as the "[[Freetown Reserve]]" was created on Tatooine and spread to a lounge elsewhere in [[the galaxy]].<ref name="HyperspaceLoungeMenu">''[[Star Wars: Hyperspace Lounge]]'' menu, on {{WebCite|url=https://disneycruiselineblog.com/menus/menu-viewer/?Menu=231&Version=771|text=Star Wars: Hyperspace Lounge Beverage Menu|work=disneycruiselineblog.com|archivedate=20240915143330}}</ref>

